			"notes": "This release does a few things:\n\n- Adds a dependency on [GeckoLib](https://geckolib.com/) in order to allow for custom armor textures, because, as I said in the last release, mixins are hard.\n- Completely refactors the codebase to make it much, much quicker to add new armors. New armors can now be created in \"one line\" of code through use of the `ArmorItemFactory`. For example, say you've created a new item--call it Lazium--you can create a new set of Lazium armor by simply adding a line to the `Armors` class:\n\n```java\npublic static final Map<String, Item> LAZIUM = ArmorItemFactory.makeArmorSet(\"lazium\").getItemsForRegistration();\n```\n\nIf you then throw your `LAZIUM` into the [`allItems()`](https://github.com/OpenBagTwo/UnobtainiumArmor/blob/d3f5c7ed58116f6ec947f88a314722c20124fd45/src/main/java/net/openbagtwo/unobtainiumarmor/items/Armors.java#L109) method a few lines down, you've got a brand new crafting ingredient and armor set added to your mod (textures not included, but there is a [Python notebook](https://github.com/OpenBagTwo/UnobtainiumArmor/blob/d3f5c7ed58116f6ec947f88a314722c20124fd45/Armor%20File%20Generator.ipynb) for generating all the JSON cruft).\n\nThis `ArmorItemFactory` provides a whole host of additional \"builder\" methods for customizing your armor's attributes (the defaults are the values for iron), replacing the armor model with a Mythril model (shamelessly stolen from [a tutorial by Kaupenjoe](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sKYxOSiINuw) or adding an armored elytra. Plenty of examples are provided, so if you're looking to adapt or build on this mod, you should be in good shape."
		},
